# Security

- Never expose secrets, tokens, private keys, or credentials in source, logs, or client bundles.
- Never place Supabase service-role keys (or equivalent privileged credentials) in Flutter or Next.js clients.
- Do not log sensitive personal data, auth tokens, or secrets.
- Authorization is enforced server-side in NestJS — UI hiding is not authorization.
- Operational files are private; use authorized short-lived access only.
- Apply least privilege to credentials, database roles, and production access.
